# e2e/chips-clickable.spec.ts — the operator, 2026-11-02, on Cephalid Breakfast: "the ability chips
# eventually start to cover the two cards". The trailer's Breakfast board (Cephalid Illusionist,
# Nomads en-Kor, three duals) with a library of Islands, so each mill trigger asks nothing. Alice
# holds priority (Full control) and activates Nomads en-Kor at Cephalid Illusionist again and again:
# every round puts the activation and Cephalid's mill trigger on the stack as two more chips. Bob
# holds a Lightning Bolt with two Mountains up, so when alice passes he has a real window of his own,
# his lands clickable on his board, before the top of the stack resolves.
